<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Ukrainian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1919</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Ukrainian War was fought from November 1918 to July 1919 over Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, after the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>. It began with fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> between Polish residents and the forces of the West Ukrainian People's Republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> won, occupied all of Eastern Galicia and the Lemko lands, and the Ukrainian government and army withdrew across the Zbruch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-ukrainian-war.jpg" alt="Polish–Ukrainian War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Дмитро Вортман, Максим Майоров, Леонід Криницький · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:02._%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%BE-%D1%83%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B0_1918-1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
